.Dd February 26, 2026
.Dt SORT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sort
.Nd sort lines of text files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bdfginrhsuczCV
.Op Fl k Ar keydef
.Op Fl t Ar char
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl Fl check Ns Op = Ns Ar type
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility sorts lines read from the specified
.Ar file
operands, or from standard input if no files are specified,
and writes the result to standard output.
.Pp
If a
.Ar file
is
.Ql - ,
.Nm
reads from standard input.
.Pp
Comparisons are performed according to the current locale's
collating sequence when no options are given.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b , Fl Fl ignore-leading-blanks
Ignore leading blanks when finding sort keys in each line.
.It Fl d , Fl Fl dictionary-order
Consider only blanks and alphanumeric characters in comparisons.
.It Fl f , Fl Fl ignore-case
Fold lowercase characters to uppercase for comparison.
.It Fl g , Fl Fl general-numeric-sort
Compare according to general numeric value.
Converts a prefix of each line to a floating-point number
for comparison, handling scientific notation.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl human-numeric-sort
Compare human-readable numbers (e.g., 2K, 1G).
.It Fl i , Fl Fl ignore-nonprinting
Consider only printable characters in comparisons.
.It Fl n , Fl Fl numeric-sort
Compare according to string numerical value.
Leading blanks and the optional sign are stripped.
.It Fl r , Fl Fl reverse
Reverse the result of comparisons.
.It Fl k Ar keydef , Fl Fl key Ns = Ns Ar keydef
Sort via the specified key definition.
.Ar keydef
has the form
.Sm off
.Ar F
.Op .C
.Op Ar opts
.Op , Ar F
.Op .C
.Op Ar opts
.Sm on
where
.Ar F
is a field number and
.Ar C
a character position within the field, both origin 1.
.Ar opts
is one or more of the letters
.Cm bdfinrhg
to override the global sort options for this key.
Multiple
.Fl k
options may be given to define primary, secondary, etc. keys.
.It Fl t Ar char , Fl Fl field-separator Ns = Ns Ar char
Use
.Ar char
as the field separator.
Without this option, fields are delimited by runs of blanks.
.It Fl u , Fl Fl unique
With
.Fl c ,
check for strict ordering.
Without
.Fl c ,
output only the first of equal-comparing lines.
.It Fl s , Fl Fl stable
Stabilize the sort, disabling last-resort comparison.
.It Fl c , Fl Fl check , Fl Fl check Ns = Ns Cm diagnose-first
Check whether input is sorted.
Do not sort; output a diagnostic for the first out-of-order line.
.It Fl C , Fl Fl check Ns = Ns Cm quiet , Fl Fl check Ns = Ns Cm silent
Like
.Fl c
but do not report the first bad line.
Exit with status 1 if the input is not sorted.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl Fl output Ns = Ns Ar file
Write output to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl z , Fl Fl zero-terminated
Use NUL as the line delimiter instead of newline.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.It Fl Fl help
Display help information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success, 1 if the
.Fl c
or
.Fl C
check finds disorder, and 2 if an error occurs.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sort a file alphabetically:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort names.txt
.Pp
Sort numerically in reverse order:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort -nr scores.txt
.Pp
Sort by the second field using colon as separator:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort -t: -k2,2 /etc/passwd
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr comm 1 ,
.Xr join 1 ,
.Xr uniq 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Pp
The
.Fl g , h , V , z
options and
.Fl Fl check Ns = Ns Cm quiet
are GNU extensions.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
